285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 115 0 R
/E (Thus, this behavior validates the ResNet as a reasonably well-trained model.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (Changing the optimizer moved the models from clear underfitting to solid performance. Then, data augmentation helped reduce the gap between training and test accuracy. This was especially evident in the AlexNet case, where, after the architectural modification, the model developed a large and persistent generalization gap: training accuracy kept improving while test accuracy stagnated. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (Overall, this suggests that some architectural changes may have been suboptimal, and that keeping the standard network configuration \(while improving the training setup\) could likely have achieved comparable results.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (Finally, by further analyzing the predictions of both final models, we observed that the remaining errors are mostly class confusions driven by visual similarity between categories and some level of dataset noise. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (However, the models tend to make mistakes more frequently on particular classes, so maybe a further step could be to investigate the reason why the model has more error in one class than an other and the most common class confusion error. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (The next round of improvements should therefore focus on those problematic classes, investigating whether the issue is: )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 514 0 R
/E (option 1:  insufficient diversity/representation \(the model learns too few features for those classes\);)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 515 0 R
/E (option 2:  overly aggressive augmentation that may have distorted already ambiguous examples and obstacled learning.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
